# The committed engine artifacts under build/ are binary — no line-ending normalization,
# no textconv. Their byte-identity is enforced by scripts/check-wireguard-core-drift.sh,
# which is also the compensating control for build/'s exclusion from the textual
# QA-enablement scan (scripts/check-public-qa-enablement.mjs).
#
# Deliberately OUTSIDE build/. Living inside it made this file unverifiable: it is
# hand-maintained, so the rebuild preserved it byte-for-byte and it matched in both drift
# manifests; it sat in the scan-excluded tree, so nothing read it; and its own `* binary`
# rule matched itself, so even an ordinary `git diff` of it was opaque. A file that governs
# how the artifacts are stored should not be one of the things the artifact gate cannot see.
build/** binary
